course: dictionary
lesson: 4177
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. Going can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, and its meaning changes a little each time. The words around it show you which job it is doing. «I'm going to the park» means travelling somewhere.
explain: Look at what comes next. «I'm going to read» uses going to with another verb to show a plan or the future. «The going was hard» uses going as a noun, meaning how easy or hard it is to make progress.
explain: Going can also mean available or usual now, as in «the best one going». In phrases, a word can take on a new meaning too: «keep going» means do not stop. Ask yourself which job going is doing in the sentence, then check that your meaning fits.
fact: Going is a verb, a noun and an adjective.
fact: «Going to» plus a verb shows a plan or the future, as in «I'm going to read».
fact: «Get going» means start, and «keep going» means don't stop.
fact: «Going, going, gone!» is what an auctioneer says before selling something.
fact: «Comings and goings» means people arriving and leaving.
exercise: «I'm going to read my new book after tea.» What does going to show here? | Stopping at once | Moving very slowly | Travelling to the library | *A plan for what will happen next
exercise: «Keep going, you are nearly at the top!» What does keep going mean? | Sleep for a while | Turn around and go home | *Do not stop | Leave the race now
exercise: «The going was hard through the thick mud.» What job is going doing here? | *A noun: how hard it was to make progress | A verb meaning leaving home | An adjective meaning usual | A plan for the future
test: «Put the kettle on, we need to get going.» What does get going mean? | Count to ten | *Start | Run away from home | Stop and rest
test: «Is there any bread going?» What does going mean here? | Moving away | A plan for later | *Available right now | A slow walk
exam: In the phrase «comings and goings», what do the words mean? | *People arriving and leaving | Long journeys by train | Old stories from long ago | Things said quietly
